or closed; OQ-1 and OQ-2 open questions that Phase 1 states do not block).

Evidence at declaration:
  20 .proto files compile and lint clean
  649 generated files across rust, swift, kotlin, csharp
  all four bindings COMPILE against their pinned runtimes
  35801 contract checks, 0 failures
  201 reason codes across 16 domains; 28 capabilities; 12 canonical states

What this file authorizes: production implementation under ADR-0018 §11.12's
repository layout may begin.

What it does NOT authorize: any change to contracts/. The freeze procedure in
the Phase 3 objective still applies — a contract may change only on a
demonstrated defect, documented, reviewed by the integration lead, checked for
Phase 1 and compatibility implications, explicitly approved, with contract tests
updated and this decision amended. Implementation inconvenience is not a reason.

If the schema changes, scripts/check_freeze_scope.py fails until this file is
re-declared deliberately.
